# Reeds / cattails: tall stands on the banks and in the shallows of SLOW water - a river's calm reaches, its pools, a
# lake's shore. Long leaves from the root (the stem's colours) around a stalk with a brown cattail spike. Format:
# Code/Procedural/CONTEXT.md, "Ground clutter".
ClutterType Reed
	Kind Flower
	Seed 211
	Scale 0.75 1.3
	Range 120
	Color 0.30 0.45 0.18
	Color2 0.30 0.18 0.09
	Head Reed
	Petals 16
	Open 12
	# the leaves PetalWidth x HeadSize wide (4.5 cm), the cattail HeadSize long, a tenth of it wide
	PetalWidth 0.15
	Stem 1.7
	HeadSize 0.3
	Placement
		Density 20
		Temperature 2 35
		# along a river or a lake (1 in the channel, 0 past its floodplain), and only where the water runs slowly
		# curve 4: close to the water (half way across the floodplain ~6 %)
		River 0 1 4
		Flow 1 0.2
		# at the water's edge, a few out in the shallows
		Water 1 0.001
		Cluster 10 0.75
		Slope 0.5
		Altitude -1000
